From 441a5464ba0abc0093564ae1454de3e09a008728 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:48:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(process): persist_on_release jobs survive gateway
 restarts and Kanban run-scope stops [daveey]

Hub 2026-11-03: paid GPU-rental watchdogs started by Kanban workers with
persist_on_release died with gateway restarts and worker OOMs, leaving rentals
billing unsupervised.

- The next gateway adopted the orphaned worker job from processes.json, and its
  next shutdown swept it with kill_all(source="gateway_shutdown"), which reaches
  persisted jobs. A restart now sweeps with the lifecycle source
  "gateway_restart", which spares persisted jobs (the next gateway re-adopts
  them). A real stop still kills the persisted jobs it spawned (#41225/#46778),
  but never one it only adopted.
- A worker's run scope (OOMPolicy=stop, KillMode=control-group) is stopped on
  an OOM or after the run, which took its persisted jobs with it. A
  persist_on_release job spawned in a Kanban run scope now gets its own
  transient scope in hermes-kanban.slice, with the run scope's memory cap.
- format_uptime_short moved to tools/process_registry_uptime.py (line cap).
